n the United Kingdom (UK) in 2020, by market share. With reference to the information on the preceding page, explain the market structure of mortgage lending in the UK.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["market structure","concentration ratio","mortgage lenders","market share"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 5 as printed"},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2024-jun-q5b","p":5,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(b)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"The graph below shows the largest mortgage lenders in the United Kingdom (UK) in 2020, by market share. The value of all mortgage loans was £1 601 billion at the end of 2020. Which one of the following is the value of Lloyds’ market share?","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["market share","mortgage lenders","calculation"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 5 as printed","type":"mcq","options":["£82 billion","£126 billion","£312 billion","£8 210 billion"],"usesFigure":true},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2023-jun-q6a","p":4,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(a)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"With reference to Figure 1, explain the market structure that best describes the market for UK online streaming services.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["market structure","oligopoly","streaming","Netflix"],"qpPage":15,"msPage":10,"ctxPage":13,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2023-jun-q2c","p":22,"section":"B","questionNumber":"2(c)","parentQuestion":"2","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"Discuss possible methods of price and non‑price competition that firms could use to increase the value of sales on the high street.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly","3-3-1-revenue"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["price competition","non-price competition","retail","revenue"],"qpPage":21,"msPage":20,"ctxPage":19,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2022-jun-q4a","p":3,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(a)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"Pilgrim’s Pride is the second-largest chicken supplier in the US. It will pay a $107.9 million fine for price fixing with Tyson Foods and other chicken suppliers. The firms limited production to force prices higher and harm major customers, including KFC. Pilgrim’s Pride is thought to have gained at least $361 million in total revenue from the collusion. Draw a simple two firm/two outcome game theory model to show why the chicken suppliers may have colluded.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["game theory","collusion","price fixing","payoff matrix"],"qpPage":8,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2022-jun-q4b","p":3,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(b)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"Pilgrim’s Pride is the second-largest chicken supplier in the US. It will pay a $107.9 million fine for price fixing with Tyson Foods and other chicken suppliers. The firms limited production to force prices higher and harm major customers, including KFC. Pilgrim’s Pride is thought to have gained at least $361 million in total revenue from the collusion. Which one of the following is most closely associated with tacit collusion?","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["tacit collusion","oligopoly","price fixing"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 4 as printed","type":"mcq","options":["Overt sharing of information","Predatory pricing","Price wars","Unspoken agreements"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2022-jun-q5c","p":3,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(c)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"The makers of Fiat cars merged with the makers of Vauxhall cars in 2021. Fiat management had aggressively sought a merger to achieve economies of scale. The competition authorities in the EU investigated the merger. Explain one likely concern the EU competition authorities may have had about the merger.","topics":["3-6-1-government-intervention","3-4-4-oligopoly","3-1-2-business-growth"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["competition policy","merger","market power","car industry"],"qpPage":10,"msPage":9,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2022-jun-q6a","p":3,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(a)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"With reference to Figure 1, calculate the three-firm concentration ratio for branded coffee shop chains.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["concentration ratio","oligopoly","coffee shops","calculation"],"qpPage":15,"msPage":10,"ctxPage":14,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q8","p":7,"section":"C","questionNumber":"8","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-sec-c","marks":25,"questionText":"In many industries, such as banking, health insurance, internet search engines, pharmaceuticals, social media and telecommunications, there have been increases in market concentration. Evaluate the possible consequences for business decision making of increased market concentration. Refer to industries of your choice in your answer.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["market concentration","oligopoly","business decision making","concentration ratio"],"qpPage":30,"msPage":27,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2019-jun-q8","p":2,"section":"C","questionNumber":"8","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":"edexcel-a-p1-2019-jun-sec-c","marks":25,"questionText":"In October 2017 Scania, the Volkswagen-owned truck maker, was fined €880 million (£771 million) by the European Commission for colluding with five other truck manufacturers over a 14-year period. The firms had agreed to coordinate prices after experiencing additional costs of meeting emission regulations. With reference to an industry of your choice, evaluate why some firms engage in collusive behaviour.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["collusion","cartel","oligopoly","price fixing","game theory"],"qpPage":26,"msPage":21,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2019-jun-q1a","p":20,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(a)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"With reference to Figure 1 and Extract A, explain what is meant by a ‘highly concentrated’ market for potato crisps (Extract A, lines 2–3).","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["concentrated market","concentration ratio","oligopoly","crisps"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":4,"ctxPage":3,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2019-jun-q1c","p":20,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(c)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"In Extract A, lines 15–16, it was suggested that some firms may respond to the advertising ban by cutting the prices of their products. Using game theory and the information provided in Figure 1 and Extract A, discuss the effects on firms of cutting prices in an oligopolistic market.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["game theory","price war","oligopoly","interdependence"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":6,"ctxPage":3,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2018-jun-q5c","p":1,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(c)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"The following graph shows the global sales of personal computers (PCs) between 2011 and 2015. The following table shows global sales of PCs by company in 2015. Calculate the five-firm concentration ratio. You are advised to show your working.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"